<template>
    <heading>Operations</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>operations</li>
        <li>generator</li>
        <li>coroutine</li>
        <li>event handler</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>to_handler</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>operations</code> holds the application's multi-step event handlers. Each handler is a generator object, created and primed by <code>to_handler</code>. The generator receives <code>self</code>, a function that returns its own object; calling <code>self()</code> after construction avoids accessing the object before it exists.</p>
        <p>Each operation can produce one of three outcomes when <code>controller</code> resumes it with <code>handler.next(event)</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><code>yield self()</code>: remain the current handler. The controller stops dispatching this event; the next event resumes the same operation.</li>
            <li><code>yield child</code>, where <code>child</code> is another primed generator object: call a child operation. The controller pushes <code>child</code> onto <code>handlerStack</code> and immediately dispatches the same event to it.</li>
            <li><code>return</code>, or reach the end of the generator: finish the operation. The generator result has <code>done === true</code>, so the controller pops it and resumes the parent with the same event. Any returned value is ignored. If no parent remains, dispatch ends.</li>
        </ol>
        <p><code>baseOperationsHandler</code> receives events and normally ignores them, yielding <code>self()</code> to remain the current handler. When it receives <code>"ModalDialog"</code>, it pushes a primed <code>modalDialogOperation</code> as a child handler. The stub consumes that event and remains the current handler. <code>operations</code> installs the primed base handler with <code>controller.init(handler)</code> before any events are dispatched.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Outermost scope objects</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
let operations = (() => {
    function to_handler(generator) {
        const handler = generator(() => handler);
        handler.next();
        return handler;
    }

    function* modalDialogOperation(self) {
        while (true) {
            let event = yield self();
        }
    }

    function* baseOperationsHandler(self) {
        while (true) {
            let event = yield self();
            if (event === "ModalDialog")
                yield to_handler(modalDialogOperation);
        }
    }

    const handler = to_handler(baseOperationsHandler);
    controller.init(handler);

    return {};
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
